<Project>

  <!--
    Whether this build contains the UI Automation bridge at all.

    THE BRIDGE IS A REMOTELY INVOCABLE COMMAND CHANNEL INTO APPLICATION LOGIC.

    UI Automation has no per-caller authentication: any process at the same or higher
    integrity level on the same desktop can enumerate the tree, find the fragment root
    and call the pattern. There is no permission to check and no caller to identify, so
    absence is the only control that actually holds. A shipping build must therefore
    contain no bridge code - not disabled code, absent code.

    ON FOR Debug, OFF FOR EVERYTHING ELSE.

    Debug is the configuration the UI test suite builds and runs, and Release is what
    ships; inventing a third configuration would mean teaching every tool in the repo
    about it to express a distinction those two already draw. Override deliberately with
    -p:BrinellUiaBridge=true|false, which is how the gating test builds an uninstrumented
    host without leaving Debug.

    IMPORTED, NOT COPIED, ON PURPOSE.

    Both ends of the bridge compile the provider sources - the app under test through
    Brinell.Maui.AppSupport, the bridge's own host through a project reference - and the
    two must agree about whether the provider exists. Two copies of this rule would
    eventually disagree, and the symptom would be a runtime "nothing answers" rather than
    a build error.

    COPYING BrinellMauiAppSupport INTO AN APP: the constant does not come with the files.
    An app that copies the sources in gets no bridge until it defines BRINELL_UIA_BRIDGE
    itself, which is the safe direction for a gate to fail in.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <BrinellUiaBridge Condition="'$(BrinellUiaBridge)' == '' AND '$(Configuration)' == 'Debug'">true</BrinellUiaBridge>
    <BrinellUiaBridge Condition="'$(BrinellUiaBridge)' == ''">false</BrinellUiaBridge>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(BrinellUiaBridge)' == 'true'">
    <DefineConstants>$(DefineConstants);BRINELL_UIA_BRIDGE</DefineConstants>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
